 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the Huntington\nunion free school district notwithstanding the failure to timely file final\nbuilding cost reports with the education department",
    "basePrintNo": "S7038",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7038-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7038\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm the actions of the\nHuntington union free school district notwithstanding the failure to\ntimely file final building cost reports with the education department\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nLegalizes, validates, ratifies and confirms the actions of the Hunting-\nton Union Free School District regardless of the failure of the State\nEducation Department (SED) to locate final building cost reports that\nhad been timely filed.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Allows the Education Department to consider the final cost\nreport for Huntington Union Free School District as legalized, vali-\ndated, ratified and confirmed for approved building projects completed\nprior to December 31, 2011, recognizing that the failure to file the\nreport in a timely manner was an inadvertent administrative or minister-\nial oversight by SED.\n\nSection 2: Provides that the Commissioner of the State Education Depart-\nment shall not recover from the Huntington Union Free School District\nany penalty arising from the late filing of a final cost report pursuant\nto section 31 of part A of chapter 57 of the laws of 2012, provided that\nany amounts already so recovered shall be deemed a payment for money due\nfor prior years pursuant to paragraph c of subdivision 5 of section 3604\nof the Education Law and shall be paid to the Huntington Union Free\nSchool District pursuant to such provision.\n\nSection 3: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Huntington Union Free School District submitted three final cost\nreport packages in 2011 all on the same date. The State Education\nDepartment confirmed that two of the three packages were received. In\nthe meantime, the school district had a number of staff turnovers,\nincluding the Assistant Superintendent for Business, and the senior\naccountant. In 2013, the school district noticed that a number of cost\nreports did not show up as being filed. The Facilities Planning staff\ntold the District they were having difficulty with lost reports. The DOE\nFacilities Planning staff eventually located a number of these reports,\nor the District was able to show they had been mailed.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.2976 - 2019- Veto No. 129\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
